    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0798" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1953: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-09T15:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                                1921—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 10—4:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1. I have held extensive conference with both Zayas<anchor n="9" xml:id="d646-f1"
                    /> and Gómez<anchor n="10" xml:id="d646-f2"/> and with adherents of each. I
                    understand in sufficient detail the status of the contested election cases
                    before the court. I have a plan for expediting court action which I will
                    formulate tonight and submit to President Menocal tomorrow morning. In brief
                    outline it means rules of procedure to be promulgated by the Central Electoral
                    Board governing courts in their hearings of these cases. I have given
                    preliminary consideration to congested dock situation and to financial
                    matters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d646-f1" n="9" xml:id="d646-f1-content">
                <p>Dr. Alfredo Zayas, Vice President of the Republic of Cuba; Liga Coalition
                    candidate for President.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d646-f2" n="10" xml:id="d646-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. Jose Miguel Gémez, ex-President of the Republic of Cuba; Liberal candidate
                    for President.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
